                "error: a value is required for '{}' but none was supplied\\n\\n{}\\n",
                opt_name,
                tip_more_info()
            ),
            exit_code: 2,
        }),
    }
}"""
new2 = """fn take_value<I: Iterator<Item = String>>(
    inline: Option<String>,
    args: &mut std::iter::Peekable<I>,
    opt_name: &str,
) -> Result<String, ParseResult> {
    if let Some(v) = inline {
        return Ok(v);
    }
    // If next arg looks like another option, report it as unexpected.
    if let Some(v) = args.peek() {
        if v.len() > 1 && v.starts_with('-') && v != "-" {
            let bad = v.clone();
            return Err(err_unexpected(&bad));
        }
    }
    match args.next() {
        Some(v) => Ok(v),
        None => Err(ParseResult::Err {
            message: format!(
                "error: a value is required for '{}' but none was supplied\\n\\n{}\\n",
                opt_name,
                tip_more_info()
            ),
            exit_code: 2,
        }),
    }
}"""
